            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "reopened https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40422 as a mitigation, but hopefully we can find a more general fix.\n\nhopefully there's some way in C to change the \"tostring\" form of `vim.NIL` so that it reports `vim.NIL` instead of `vim.NIL`. then any time it's reported in an error message, instead of:\n\n    E5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: bad argument #1 to 'pairs' (table expected, got userdata)\n\nit reports:\n\n    E5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: bad argument #1 to 'pairs' (table expected, got vim.NIL)\n\n",
